WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.251 --> 00:00:07.835
Aisha Coleman: Morning, Linda. How's the week treating you up in Tacoma?

2
00:00:08.264 --> 00:00:13.592
Linda Sorensen: Oh, you know. Rain since Monday. My commute's been a swim. How about you?

3
00:00:13.988 --> 00:00:21.553
Aisha Coleman: Same story down here, minus the ferry. I saw the Mariners thing on your LinkedIn, that member event looked fun.

4
00:00:22.595 --> 00:00:33.482
Linda Sorensen: It was. We had a booth at the Tacoma fall festival, and honestly half the people who stopped by just wanted the free tote bags.

5
00:00:33.961 --> 00:00:44.806
Aisha Coleman: Um, Classic. Okay, so I know we've got a short window. I wanted to to check in ahead of renewal season and hear how things are sitting with you and the team.

6
00:00:46.084 --> 00:00:58.099
Linda Sorensen: Yeah. Overall the platform's doing what we need. Call volumes have been steady, we're around nine thousand a month across the the branches and the lending line, little bump when rates move.

7
00:00:58.849 --> 00:01:05.817
Aisha Coleman: That tracks with what I see on the tracking numbers. Anything shift on the staffing side since summer?

8
00:01:07.243 --> 00:01:16.078
Linda Sorensen: We finally filled the two member service rep roles on the evening shift. Took four I mean, months. Uh, so the queue's breathing again, which is nice.

9
00:01:17.093 --> 00:01:19.996
Aisha Coleman: Good. I I know that was a grind.

10
00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:32.331
Linda Sorensen: Mm. And the QM side, we're still scoring everything, compliance reviews every scorecard change before it goes live, so that process is slow but it's working.

11
00:01:33.079 --> 00:01:37.236
Aisha Coleman: Understood. No changes to the scorecards since we last talked?

12
00:01:37.476 --> 00:01:48.414
Linda Sorensen: No, not right now. It's fine. Honestly, the thing that's actually on my plate um, is the renewal conversation. And it's not really coming from me.

13
00:01:49.537 --> 00:01:51.204
Aisha Coleman: Okay. Tell me more.

14
00:01:52.394 --> 00:02:12.752
Linda Sorensen: So finance and procurement have been going through every vendor contract since the third quarter. And they've landed on this idea that they don't want to keep paying separately for things that feel like add-ons. PreSense, the QM seats, AI Voice Agent minutes, all of it. They want one bundled price. One number on the page.

15
00:02:14.244 --> 00:02:21.488
Aisha Coleman: Got it. And is that a hard line from them, or is it more of a preference going into the negotiation?

16
00:02:21.725 --> 00:02:32.814
Linda Sorensen: It's It's pretty firm. I I sat in a meeting Tuesday, and the procurement lead, her name's Diane, she said she doesn't want to see four line items on a renewal.

17
00:02:32.814 --> 00:02:39.969
Linda Sorensen: She wants to see I mean, one. So when the renewal comes up in February, that's the shape they're expecting.

18
00:02:40.608 --> 00:02:47.577
Aisha Coleman: That's helpful. Can I ask, is it the total dollar amount that's the issue, or the structure?

19
00:02:47.847 --> 00:02:55.763
Linda Sorensen: Structure, mostly. The number itself we can work with. It's the feeling that every time we turn around there's another meter running.

20
00:02:55.763 --> 00:02:57.562
Linda Sorensen: That's what they're reacting to.

21
00:02:57.978 --> 00:03:17.386
Aisha Coleman: Okay. I don't want to promise anything on the spot, because packaging isn't something I set. What I can do is take this to our deal desk with the specifics, the seat count, the minutes, and the PreSense usage, and see what a bundled structure could look like.

22
00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:24.785
Linda Sorensen: That's all I'm asking. I just need something to put in front of Diane that doesn't look like a phone bill.

23
00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:28.499
Aisha Coleman: Fair. When do you need it by?

24
00:03:29.698 --> 00:03:34.673
Linda Sorensen: If I could have something by mid-November, that gives me room before the holidays.

25
00:03:34.928 --> 00:03:49.331
Aisha Coleman: Mid-November works. Uh, Let me get the usage numbers from our side first so I'm not guessing. I'll email you a summary by Wednesday and then we can get on a call with whoever needs to be on it.

26
00:03:50.565 --> 00:04:00.896
Linda Sorensen: Perfect. And Aisha, just so you know, I'm not trying to squeeze anyone. I like working with you. This is Diane's process, not mine.

27
00:04:01.813 --> 00:04:05.465
Aisha Coleman: I know. And I'd rather hear it now than in February.

28
00:04:06.054 --> 00:04:20.944
Linda Sorensen: Right. Oh, one other thing. Our Salesforce admin, Priya, she's rolling out some new reporting for the you know, member experience team, so if you get questions from her about call data fields, that's what it's about.

29
00:04:21.546 --> 00:04:25.060
Aisha Coleman: Um, Good to know. I'll keep an eye out.

30
00:04:26.088 --> 00:04:31.023
Linda Sorensen: And the Google Ads side is uh, still plugging along. Nothing new there.

31
00:04:31.435 --> 00:04:34.362
Aisha Coleman: Great. Anything else before I let you go?

32
00:04:35.413 --> 00:04:39.619
Linda Sorensen: No, that's the uh, big one. Thanks for hearing me out.

33
00:04:41.073 --> 00:04:47.024
Aisha Coleman: Of course. I'll get you that summary Wednesday, and we'll talk packaging after that.

34
00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:49.020
Linda Sorensen: Sounds good. Stay dry.

35
00:04:50.270 --> 00:04:51.987
Aisha Coleman: You too. Talk soon, Linda.
